@ Index:   Loads cube, prime and pi test data
@ Author:  Jaco Mostert
@ Previous Standard test data, registers 10 to 38, loaded by hand.
@ Tested:  XEQ ‘tstData’
@ Input:   none
@ Output:  R11=569936821221962380720, R22=18014398241046527, R34 the 101-digit pi*10^100
LBL ‘tstData’
  ‘Reg 11, 12 & 13 have: The 3 cubes = 3.’
  STO R10
  569936821221962380720
  STO R11
  -569936821113563493509
  STO R12
  -472715493453327032
  STO R13
  ‘Reg 15, 16 & 17 have: The 3 cubes = 42.’
  STO R14
  -80538738812075974
  STO R15
  80435758145817515
  STO R16
  12602123297335631
  STO R17
  ‘37 digits of pi, Reg19 / Reg20.’
  STO R18
  2646693125139304345
  STO R19
  842468587426513207
  STO R20
  ‘Primes: Carol’
  STO R21
  18014398241046527
  STO R22
  ‘Primes: Kynea’
  STO R23
  18446744082299486207
  STO R24
  ‘Primes: repunit’
  STO R25
  7369130657357778596659
  STO R26
  ‘Primes: Woodal’
  STO R27
  195845982777569926302400511
  STO R28
  ‘Primes: Woodal’
  STO R29
  4776913109852041418248056622882488319
  STO R30
  ‘Primes: Woodal’
  STO R31
  225251798594466661409915431774713195745814267044878909733007331390393510002687
  STO R32
  ‘pi.(10^100) (101 digits) longinteger’
  STO R33
  31415926535897932384626433832795028841971693993751058209749445923078164062862089986280348253421170680
  STO R34
  ‘100 primes product 2×3×...×541’
  STO R36
  4711930799906184953162487834760260422020574773409675520188634839616415335845034221205289256705544681972439104097777157991804380284218315038719444943990492579030720635990538452312528339864352999310398481791730017201031090
  STO R37
  ‘Heart:16×(sin(t)^3)+i×(13×cos(t)-5×cos(2×t)-2×cos(3×t)-cos(4×t))’
